ndness it's firing the coach who says  you are so weak and hiring the one who  says I understand it's tough when your  team is getting blown out at halftime  you don't win the game by screaming you  suck  coach Kade the legendary Duke basketball  coach with the most wins in division 1  men's basketball history says that his  most reliable pep talk to his players is  I believe in you the positive impact of  self-compassion is rooted in biology  when we are hard on ourselves our body  doesn't realize that it's our self-talk  and not someone else yelling at us and  releases stress hormones when you stew  on that problem or beat yourself up over  that failure your body continues to  release cortisol diverting energy from a  task at hand that's why if you are a  basketball player and you miss the first  free throw  you don't improve your chances of making  the next one by beating yourself up you  do it by taking a deep breath and  concentrating as one of the greatest  poets of our generation Taylor Swift  fill this you need to just shake it off  last week I cut myself thinking I am not  strong enough to give this talk I have  too much going on it's going to be so  bad I am at this appointment but that's  a lie I am strong enough but it's not  about strength I was drunk on cortisol  and I needed to get my head back in the  game so how do they do it  four years ago I wouldn't have I would  have kept beating myself up all the way  to a very mediocre draft in the turbo  self-fulfilling prophecy today when I  realize I'm being myself up I bring up  my inner scotch K who says I believe in  you and I go through five steps of self  compassion first name it mean what it is  that you're actually feeling I wasn't  just stressed I was hurting because with  everything else going on with my  life I didn't feel I had capacity to do  justice to a topic that matters so much  to me need to first understand exactly  what's wrong step 2  feel it allow yourself to fully embrace  that feeling